I'd like to talk about a childhood friend of mine named Wing.

I first met him when I was a child because we lived in the same neighborhood. We also went to the same school and were in the same class for several years, so we naturally became very close friends.

Wing was an intelligent and friendly person who never failed to make me laugh. One of my favorite memories with him was playing video games together at Internet cafés. This was when we were in grade 6. At that time, he knew a lot about computers and online games, whereas I was still a beginner. He patiently showed me how to set up the games, explained different strategies, and even taught me some useful tricks to improve my gameplay.

We usually spent about an hour or two playing together after school. Thanks to his guidance, my gaming skills improved significantly, and we often won matches as a team. What I enjoyed most was that he was incredibly creative and always came up with new tactics that caught me by surprise.

Besides being fun to be around, Wing was also a very hardworking and responsible student. He dreamed of studying engineering at a prestigious university, so he took his studies seriously. Even though he loved playing games, he always made time for self-study and often attended extra classes to strengthen his knowledge. As a result, he consistently achieved excellent academic results and was one of the top students in our class.

Unfortunately, we lost touch when his family moved to another city during middle school. Although we no longer keep in contact, I still remember him fondly because he played an important role in my childhood and made those years much more enjoyable.
